From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:45:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] module-droid-card: never start in a virtual profile

module-card-restore saves the card profile whenever it changes, so a
PulseAudio that goes down during a call - an abort, a restart, the
device losing power - comes back with the virtual "voicecall" profile
saved, and restores it while the card is being created. Before the card
is linked pa_card_set_profile() only sets active_profile, so
card_set_profile() never runs, u->real_profile stays NULL, and
init_profile() then reads the virtual profile's mapping sets, which do
not exist - add_virtual_profile() allocates the droid profile with
pa_xnew0() and never creates them:

  Assertion 's' failed at src/pulsecore/idxset.c:572,
  function pa_idxset_size(). Aborting.

The abort happens before card-restore can save anything else, so every
restart aborts the same way until the card database is removed by hand.

A virtual profile is only meaningful on top of the real profile it was
entered from. If the initial profile is a virtual one, start in the real
profile PulseAudio would have chosen instead - the same pick as
pa_card_choose_initial_profile() - and leave the call mode to whoever
runs the call, which sets it again.
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/droid/module-droid-card.c | 51 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 51 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/droid/module-droid-card.c b/src/droid/module-droid-card.c
index addebf4..e23cf46 100644
--- a/src/droid/module-droid-card.c
+++ b/src/droid/module-droid-card.c
@@ -401,6 +401,56 @@ static void add_profiles(struct userdata *u, pa_hashmap *h, pa_hashmap *ports) {
     }
 }
 
+static bool profile_is_virtual(pa_card_profile *cp) {
+    const struct profile_data *d = PA_CARD_PROFILE_DATA(cp);
+
+    return d->virtual_profile;
+}
+
+/* module-card-restore brings back the profile saved last, and that can be a
+ * virtual one: a call that was up when PulseAudio went down. A virtual profile
+ * only exists on top of the real profile it was entered from - it has no
+ * mappings of its own and u->real_profile is not set - so starting in one
+ * leaves the card without sinks and sources, and init_profile() aborts on the
+ * missing mapping sets. Start in the real profile PulseAudio would have picked
+ * instead, the way pa_card_choose_initial_profile() picks one; whoever runs
+ * the call sets the call mode again. */
+static void choose_real_initial_profile(struct userdata *u) {
+    pa_card_profile *cp, *best = NULL;
+    void *state;
+
+    pa_assert(u);
+
+    if (!profile_is_virtual(u->card->active_profile))
+        return;
+
+    PA_HASHMAP_FOREACH(cp, u->card->profiles, state) {
+        if (profile_is_virtual(cp) || cp->available == PA_AVAILABLE_NO)
+            continue;
+
+        if (!best || cp->priority > best->priority)
+            best = cp;
+    }
+
+    if (!best) {
+        PA_HASHMAP_FOREACH(cp, u->card->profiles, state) {
+            if (profile_is_virtual(cp))
+                continue;
+
+            if (!best || cp->priority > best->priority)
+                best = cp;
+        }
+    }
+
+    pa_assert(best);
+
+    pa_log_info("Not starting in virtual profile %s, using %s.", u->card->active_profile->name, best->name);
+
+    u->card->active_profile = best;
+    u->card->save_profile = false;
+    u->card->profile_is_sticky = false;
+}
+
 static void init_profile(struct userdata *u) {
     pa_droid_mapping *am;
     struct profile_data *d;
@@ -943,6 +993,7 @@ int pa__init(pa_module *m) {
     u->module = m;
 
     pa_card_choose_initial_profile(u->card);
+    choose_real_initial_profile(u);
     init_profile(u);
     u->extcon = pa_droid_extcon_new(m->core, u->card);
 
-- 
2.53.0

